WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome.
Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.067
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:06.033
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:08.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.000
Well, guys, today is
National Pharmacist Day.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.834
Yeah. To celebrate, pharmacists
everywhere were like,

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:17.334
"A Pfizer shot for you,
and a tequila shot for me.

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:19.400
Here we go.
Let's keep it going."

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.267
If you want to do something
nice for your pharmacist,

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:23.033
you can stop asking them
if they have any more

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:24.334
COVID tests in the back.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:27.567
"Everything we have is out."

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.467
Speaking of COVID tests,
the state of Florida

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:35.167
let a million COVID tests
expire in a warehouse.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:39.834
But now the FDA has decided to
extend the expiration dates.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.033
When they heard that,
every New York hot-dog vendor

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.400
was like, "Is that
really safe to do that?

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.801
Because..."

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.701
Yeah, the FDA just extended
the expiration dates.

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:58.667
When they heard that,
the CDC said,

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:01.667
"Hey, making up rules
as you go is our thing."

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:04.534
Meanwhile, Florida was like,
"You can put any date

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:05.567
on them if you want.

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:06.601
We're still not
going to use them.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.367
We don't care. We don't..."

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.434
Now, get this.

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.567
I saw that grade schools
in Massachusetts

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:14.634
are using dogs
to sniff out COVID.

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:16.534
So if the dog starts barking,

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:19.434
either you have
COVID or Lunchables.

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:25.701
[ Sniffs, growls ]

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.300
-"Bologna."
-But good news.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.300
If this works, The White House
plans to mail everyone

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.701
in the U.S. a COVID dog.

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:33.834
That's right.
So that's kind of cool.

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:35.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:39.634
Yesterday,
former President Trump

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.601
hung up during
an interview with NPR.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:45.367
[ As Trump ] I've had enough.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:48.801
[ Normal voice ]
After being challenged on

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.901
his baseless
election-fraud claims.

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:51.968
Of course,
it's not the first time

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:53.400
Trump's hung up on a phone call.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.133
I mean, we actually got ahold of
some audio from other ones.

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.934
-Really?
-Yeah. Take a listen to these.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.033
Very interesting. It's just --
-Wow!

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.601
-Quick to the trigger on that.
-Wow!

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.701
-Switching gears,
researchers found that Netflix

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:33.667
has continued to produce content
that shows people smoking,

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:36.400
despite making a pledge
that they would stop.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.634
Yeah, people don't want Netflix
to glorify addiction

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:42.667
while they watch five hours
of Netflix every night.

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.734
Netflix was like,
"We had a doll mow down

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.033
300 people in 'Squid Game.'

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.734
You're drawing
the line at smoking?

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:53.267
Okay."

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:54.767
Well, listen to this.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.701
I saw that the Oscars
are going to have a host

00:02:56.701 --> 00:02:58.868
for the first time
in four years.

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:01.033
Yeah, that will be great.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.400
Well, it turns out
a lot of celebrities

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.934
are interested in the job,
and we actually got

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:08.367
our hands on some leaked audio
of their auditions.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:09.601
Here, take a look at this.

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.601
-Oh, man.
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:14.234
I can't believe I'm hosting
the Oscars right now.

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.567
This is so crazy.

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:20.501
Okay, so, like, here are
the nominees for Best Kiss?

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:23.734
Oh, no!
I don't think that's an award.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:25.267
Kissing's, like,
pretty tight, though.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:26.267
[ Beep ]

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:27.634
-Oh, wow!
-Wow!

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:31.000
-Wow! This is just --
Look at these bright lights.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.901
-Oh, my God!
Those little statues! Wow!

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.434
-Wow!
-Wow!

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:36.767
-Wow!
[ Beep ]

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:38.868
-Great to be here on Hollywood's
biggest night, brother.

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:42.501
I read on Facebook that wireless
printers give you COVID,

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:44.901
also those
Applebee's buzzers, too.

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:46.234
Anyways, the nominees for

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:49.601
Best Technical Direction
in a Short Film are, brother...

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:51.100
Oh, wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:56.968
"Wow!"
-"Wow!"

00:03:56.968 --> 00:03:57.968
-Some business news.

00:03:57.968 --> 00:04:00.567
Apparently,
DIRECTV and Dish Network

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:03.067
are once again
in talks to merge.

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.834
Yeah, it's taken a while
to reach a deal

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:07.400
because neither of them
work when it's raining.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:11.467
That's right -- DIRECTV
and Dish Network might merge,

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:13.667
and if they do,
maybe they'll be named

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:16.100
Forbes' Most Powerful Company
of 2003.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.734
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:21.033
I saw that,
this week, Pope Francis

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:25.834
went to a record shop in
downtown Rome and bought a CD.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:26.934
Yeah, I guess
he's a big music fan.

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:28.200
Can we see him?

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.133
I guess he listened to his CD
on his drive home.

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:33.100
-♪ A-B-C-D-E-F-U ♪

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.200
-Wow. Interesting.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:37.100
He likes that?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.968
I like Gayle, too.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.834
Hey, I heard that Domino's
said, this year,

00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:45.701
it's expecting unprecedented
food-cost increases.

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:46.968
Meanwhile, Papa John's was like,

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:49.267
"As long as ketchup prices
stay low, we're fine."

00:04:49.267 --> 00:04:51.534
[ Audience groans ]

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:54.534
Oh, come on. He's not watching.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.534 --> 00:04:56.234
And, finally,
a pub owner in Ireland

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:57.968
is so tired of hearing
about COVID

00:04:57.968 --> 00:04:59.834
that he's making any customer
who mentions the virus put

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:03.067
2 euros in the COVID jar.

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:05.534
Yeah, that's not to be confused
with the other COVID jar,

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:07.400
a bowl of communal peanuts.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.467
We have a great show, everyone.

